module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSaturation.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSaturation.IdealOfClosedSubscheme
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSaturation.UniformDegree
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjClosedImmersion.Quotient
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.HomogeneousAwayMapCriteria.Basic

/-!
# The ideal of equations of `V₊(I)` is the saturation of `I`

Let `A = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒜 n` be a Noetherian graded ring generated by `𝒜 1` over `𝒜 0`, let
`X = Proj 𝒜`, and let `I ⊆ A` be a homogeneous ideal. Stacks tag 0BXK asks for the ideal of
equations of the closed subscheme `V₊(I) = Proj (𝒜 ⧸ I) ⟶ X` of Constructions tag 01N0, and
answers

`I(V₊(I)) = {x ∈ A | 𝒜 N · x ⊆ I for some N ≥ 0}`,

*the saturation of `I`*; consequently a homogeneous ideal is of the form `I(Z)` for a closed
subscheme `Z ⊆ X` exactly when it equals its own saturation.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.chartFraction_mem_ker_app_projMap_quotientMk_iff`:
  the chart kernel of `V₊(I) ⟶ Proj 𝒜` — the chart function `b / f ^ n` dies on `V₊(I)` over
  `D₊(f)` exactly when some `f ^ k · b` lies in `I`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj`
  `.mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk_iff_uniform`: for a cover by standard opens of
  elements of one positive degree `d`, a homogeneous element of a degree divisible by `d` is an
  equation for `V₊(I)` exactly when each covering element has a power carrying it into `I`. No
  hypothesis on the grading.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj`
  `.exists_pow_mul_mem_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk`: an equation for `V₊(I)`
  is carried into `I` by a power of any degree-one element.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk_iff`
  and `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.coe_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk`:
  **the saturation formula** `I(V₊(I)) = {x | 𝒜 N x ⊆ I for some N}`, elementwise and as an
  equality of sets.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk_eq`:
  a saturated homogeneous ideal is the ideal of equations of its own `V₊`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.exists_closedImmersion_idealOfClosedSubscheme_eq_iff`:
  **a homogeneous ideal is of the form `I(Z)` exactly when it is saturated.**

## Implementation notes

Neither direction goes through the torsion description of the kernel of
`A ⧸ I ⟶ ⨁ Γ(Proj (𝒜 ⧸ I), 𝒪(n))`, which is what
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/Quotient.lean` computes and which would need the
comparison map `(Proj.map ψ)^* 𝒪_{Proj 𝒜}(n) ⟶ 𝒪_{Proj ℬ}(n)` of tag 01N0 part (3) to be
related to the *pulled-back* sections that `idealOfClosedSubscheme` is defined by. The route here
is the chart comparison instead, and it is the same one the source's proof of tag 0801 uses: on
the standard open `D₊(f)` of a degree-one element the ideal sheaf of `V₊(I)` is `I` localized, so
a chart function dies there exactly when a power of `f` carries its numerator into `I`
(`chartFraction_mem_ker_app_projMap_quotientMk_iff`, which is
`Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.awayToSection_mem_ker_app_projMap_iff` followed by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.HomogeneousAwayMap.awayMk_mem_ker_awayMap_iff`).

Where the Noetherian hypothesis enters is the passage from "every degree-one `f` has a power
carrying `x` into `I`" to "one whole homogeneous component `𝒜 N` carries `x` into `I`". It is the
argument of `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj`
`.exists_irrelevant_pow_le_annihilator_of_degreeSection_eq_zero` with the annihilator of `x`
replaced by the colon ideal `(I : x)`: the degree-one elements generate the irrelevant ideal
(`span_degreeOne_eq_irrelevant`), that ideal therefore lies in the radical of `(I : x)`, a
finitely generated ideal inside a radical has a power inside the ideal
(`Ideal.exists_pow_le_of_le_radical_of_fg`), and every element of `𝒜 N` lies in the `N`-th power
of the irrelevant ideal (`mem_irrelevant_pow_of_mem`). The converse direction needs no
Noetherian hypothesis, only the degree-one cover.

The inhomogeneous case of the forward direction is handled by taking the supremum, over the
finitely many homogeneous components of `x`, of the exponents the homogeneous case produces; the
backward direction reduces to the homogeneous components through
`Stacks.GradedRing.mul_mem_isHomogeneous_iff_forall_proj`, as
`saturated_idealOfClosedSubscheme` does.

The morphism `V₊(I) ⟶ Proj 𝒜` is written `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq` with the
side condition as a hypothesis rather than with the canonical proof of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isClosedImmersion_map_quotientMk` substituted, so that the statements
apply to whichever proof a consumer has at hand; the morphism does not depend on it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01N0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N0)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite HomogeneousLocalization
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.HomogeneousIdeal

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj

universe u

attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose
attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top

-- `V₊(I) ⟶ Proj 𝒮` is a closed immersion with no side condition; made an instance here so that
-- `idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq)` can be written at all.
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isClosedImmersion_map_quotientMk

variable {S σ : Type u} [CommRing S] [SetLike σ S] [AddSubgroupClass σ S]
  (𝒮 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒮] (I : HomogeneousIdeal 𝒮)
  (hq : HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (quotientGrading I) ≤
    (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant 𝒮).map (quotientMk I))

/-! ### The chart kernel of `V₊(I) ⟶ Proj 𝒜` -/

/-- **The chart kernel of `V₊(I) = Proj (𝒮 ⧸ I) ⟶ Proj 𝒮`.** For `f` homogeneous of positive
degree `d` and `b` homogeneous of degree `n · d`, the chart function `b / f ^ n` over `D₊(f)` is
carried to zero by `V₊(I) ⟶ Proj 𝒮` exactly when some `f ^ k · b` lies in `I`.

This is `Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.awayToSection_mem_ker_app_projMap_iff` at the graded
quotient map, whose kernel on the localization
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.HomogeneousAwayMap.awayMk_mem_ker_awayMap_iff` computes elementwise. -/
theorem chartFraction_mem_ker_app_projMap_quotientMk_iff {f : S} {d : ℕ} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 d)
    (hd : 0 < d) (n : ℕ) (b : 𝒮 (n • d)) :
    chartFraction 𝒮 hf n b ∈
        RingHom.ker ((Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq).app (Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f)).hom ↔
      ∃ k : ℕ, f ^ k * (b : S) ∈ I.toIdeal := by
  have h := Stacks.ProjQuotientChartIdeal.awayToSection_mem_ker_app_projMap_iff
    (quotientMk I) hq hf hd (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk 𝒮 hf n (b : S) b.2)
  rw [Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.HomogeneousAwayMap.awayMk_mem_ker_awayMap_iff] at h
  exact h.trans (exists_congr fun _ => by
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker]; exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem)

/-- **The ideal of equations of `V₊(I)`, in the degrees that are multiples of the degree of a
cover.** If the standard opens of a family of homogeneous elements of one positive degree `d`
cover `Proj 𝒮`, then a homogeneous element `z` of a degree `m · d` is an equation for `V₊(I)`
exactly when each member of the family has a power carrying `z` into `I`.

No Noetherian hypothesis and no hypothesis on the grading: the twists needed invertible are the
ones at multiples of `d`, which the cover supplies
(`algebraicGeometry_isInvertible_twistingSheaf_smul`).

This is the shape in which the chart description of `I(V₊(I))` is correct for a grading that is
not generated in degree one, and the restriction to degrees divisible by `d` is not an artefact:
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ProjSaturation/WeightedExample.lean` carries the ring
`ℚ[x, y]` with `deg x = 2`, `deg y = 3`, where `d = 6` and the element `y` of degree `3` passes
the degreewise test of Stacks tag 0BXK's general formula without being an equation for
`V₊(y²)`. -/
theorem mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk_iff_uniform {d : ℕ} (hd : 0 < d)
    {ι : Type*} (fam : ι → S) (hfam : ∀ j, fam j ∈ 𝒮 d)
    (hcov : ⨆ j, Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 (fam j) = ⊤) {m : ℕ} (z : 𝒮 (m • d)) :
    (z : S) ∈ idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq) ↔
      ∀ j : ι, ∃ k : ℕ, fam j ^ k * (z : S) ∈ I.toIdeal := by
  have hinv := algebraicGeometry_isInvertible_twistingSheaf_smul 𝒮
    (ratioLocus_eq_top_of_iSup_basicOpen_degree 𝒮 fam hfam hcov) m
  refine ⟨fun hz j => (chartFraction_mem_ker_app_projMap_quotientMk_iff 𝒮 I hq (hfam j) hd m
      z).mp (chartFraction_mem_ker_app_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 (hfam j) hd
        (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq) m z hz), fun h => ?_⟩
  refine mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_of_forall_chartFraction_mem_ker_uniform 𝒮 hd fam hfam hcov
    (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq) z fun j c hc => ?_
  refine (chartFraction_mem_ker_app_projMap_quotientMk_iff 𝒮 I hq (hfam j) hd m c).mpr ?_
  rw [show (c : S) = (z : S) from hc]
  exact h j

/-! ### The saturation formula -/

/-- The chart function of the `m`-th component of `x` over `D₊(f)`, `f` of degree one, dies on
`V₊(I)` exactly when some `f ^ k` carries that component into `I`. -/
private theorem exists_pow_mul_decompose_mem_iff {f : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 1) (x : S) (m : ℕ) :
    chartFraction 𝒮 hf m ⟨DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 x m, by simp⟩ ∈
        RingHom.ker ((Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq).app (Proj.basicOpen 𝒮 f)).hom ↔
      ∃ k : ℕ, f ^ k * (DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 x m : S) ∈ I.toIdeal :=
  chartFraction_mem_ker_app_projMap_quotientMk_iff 𝒮 I hq hf Nat.one_pos m _

/-- **A power of any degree-one element carries an equation for `V₊(I)` into `I`.** The chart
function of each homogeneous component dies on `V₊(I)` over `D₊(f)`, so a power of `f` carries
that component into `I`; the finitely many components are then handled by one common exponent. -/
theorem exists_pow_mul_mem_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) ((𝒮 1 : Set S)) = ⊤) {f : S} (hf : f ∈ 𝒮 1) (x : S)
    (hx : x ∈ idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq)) :
    ∃ k : ℕ, f ^ k * x ∈ I.toIdeal := by
  classical
  have := algebraicGeometry_isInvertible_twistingSheaf 𝒮 hgen
  have hcomp : ∀ m : ℕ, ∃ k : ℕ,
      f ^ k * ((DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 x m : S)) ∈ I.toIdeal := by
    intro m
    have hmem : (DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 x m : S) ∈
        idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq) :=
      (Ideal.IsHomogeneous.mem_iff 𝒮
        (idealOfClosedSubscheme_isHomogeneous 𝒮 (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq))).mp hx m
    exact (exists_pow_mul_decompose_mem_iff 𝒮 I hq hf x m).mp
      (chartFraction_mem_ker_app_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 hf Nat.one_pos
        (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq) m _ hmem)
  choose k hk using hcomp
  obtain ⟨K, hK⟩ : ∃ K, ∀ m ∈ (DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 x).support, k m ≤ K :=
    ⟨(DirectSum.decompose 𝒮 x).support.sup k, fun m hm => Finset.le_sup hm⟩
  refine ⟨K, ?_⟩
  rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose 𝒮 x, Finset.mul_sum]
  refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun m hm => ?_
  rw [← Nat.sub_add_cancel (hK m hm), pow_add, mul_assoc]
  exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (hk m)

/-- **The saturation formula for the ideal of equations of `V₊(I)`.** Over a Noetherian graded
ring generated by `𝒮 1` over `𝒮 0`, an element of `S` is an equation for the closed subscheme
`V₊(I) = Proj (𝒮 ⧸ I)` exactly when one whole homogeneous component `𝒮 N` multiplies it into
`I`:

`I(V₊(I)) = {x ∈ S | 𝒮 N · x ⊆ I for some N}`. -/
@[stacks 0BXK "standard_saturation"]
theorem mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk_iff [IsNoetherianRing S]
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) ((𝒮 1 : Set S)) = ⊤) (x : S) :
    x ∈ idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq) ↔
      ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 N → y * x ∈ I.toIdeal := by
  classical
  constructor
  · intro hx
    have hrad : (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant 𝒮).toIdeal ≤
        (I.toIdeal.colon (Ideal.span {x})).radical := by
      rw [← span_degreeOne_eq_irrelevant 𝒮 hgen, Ideal.span_le]
      intro g hg
      obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := exists_pow_mul_mem_of_mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk
        𝒮 I hq hgen hg x hx
      exact SetLike.mem_coe.mpr (Ideal.mem_radical_iff.mpr
        ⟨k, Ideal.mem_colon_span_singleton.mpr hk⟩)
    obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ :=
      Ideal.exists_pow_le_of_le_radical_of_fg hrad (Ideal.fg_of_isNoetherianRing _)
    exact ⟨N, fun y hy => Ideal.mem_colon_span_singleton.mp
      (hN (mem_irrelevant_pow_of_mem 𝒮 hgen N hy))⟩
  · rintro ⟨N, hN⟩
    rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose 𝒮 x]
    refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun m _ => ?_
    refine mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_of_forall_chartFraction_mem_ker 𝒮 Nat.one_pos
      (fun g : 𝒮 1 => (g : S)) (fun g => g.2)
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOne.iSup_basicOpen_degreeOne_eq_top 𝒮 hgen)
      (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq) (m := m) ⟨_, by simp⟩ fun g => ?_
    refine (exists_pow_mul_decompose_mem_iff 𝒮 I hq g.2 x m).mpr ⟨N, ?_⟩
    have hgN : (g : S) ^ N ∈ 𝒮 N := by simpa using SetLike.pow_mem_graded (A := 𝒮) N g.2
    have h := (Stacks.GradedRing.mul_mem_isHomogeneous_iff_forall_proj 𝒮 I.2 hgN x).mp
      (hN _ hgN) m
    rwa [GradedRing.proj_apply] at h

/-- **The saturation formula as an equality of sets**, the shape in which the source displays it:

`I(V₊(I)) = {x ∈ S | 𝒮 N · x ⊆ I for some N ≥ 0}`. -/
@[stacks 0BXK "standard_saturation"]
theorem coe_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk [IsNoetherianRing S]
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) ((𝒮 1 : Set S)) = ⊤) :
    ((idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq) : Ideal S) : Set S) =
      {x : S | ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 N → y * x ∈ I.toIdeal} :=
  Set.ext fun x => mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk_iff 𝒮 I hq hgen x

/-! ### Which ideals are ideals of equations -/

/-- **A saturated homogeneous ideal is the ideal of equations of its own `V₊`.** -/
theorem idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk_eq [IsNoetherianRing S]
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) ((𝒮 1 : Set S)) = ⊤)
    (hsat : ∀ x : S, (∃ N : ℕ, ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 N → y * x ∈ I.toIdeal) → x ∈ I.toIdeal) :
    idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 (Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq) = I.toIdeal :=
  Ideal.ext fun x =>
    (mem_idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk_iff 𝒮 I hq hgen x).trans
      ⟨hsat x, fun hx => ⟨0, fun _ _ => Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hx⟩⟩

include hq in
/-- **A homogeneous ideal is the ideal of equations of a closed subscheme of `Proj 𝒮` exactly
when it is saturated.** One direction is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.saturated_idealOfClosedSubscheme`, that an ideal of
equations is saturated; the other takes `Z = V₊(I)` and reads off the saturation formula.

"Saturated" is spelled as the source does, as the equality of `I` with its own saturation. -/
@[stacks 0BXK "saturated_ideals"]
theorem exists_closedImmersion_idealOfClosedSubscheme_eq_iff [IsNoetherianRing S]
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒮 0) ((𝒮 1 : Set S)) = ⊤) :
    (∃ (Z : Scheme.{u}) (i : Z ⟶ Proj 𝒮) (_ : IsClosedImmersion i),
        idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 i = I.toIdeal) ↔
      (I.toIdeal : Set S) = {x : S | ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ y : S, y ∈ 𝒮 N → y * x ∈ I.toIdeal} := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨Z, i, hi, hIeq⟩
    refine Set.ext fun x => ⟨fun hx => ⟨0, fun _ _ => Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hx⟩, fun hx => ?_⟩
    rw [← hIeq] at hx ⊢
    exact saturated_idealOfClosedSubscheme 𝒮 hgen i x hx
  · intro hsat
    exact ⟨Proj (quotientGrading I), Proj.map (quotientMk I) hq,
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isClosedImmersion_map_quotientMk I,
      idealOfClosedSubscheme_projMap_quotientMk_eq 𝒮 I hq hgen fun _ hx => hsat.ge hx⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj

end
